From b23afd2672318bc8d1f6c58ad5c76fb13ea0fb82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Minkovsky <dminkovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:37:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Read a verdict's folder check and unattended pick from its
 rows

The identify state, the pane and the pane's opening on the draft worked both
values out in Rust from the stored findings on every read. A view over the
verdict's own rows now says them: the import list's reason, the cards
statement and the pane's write all read it, so the rule has one copy in SQL
and VerdictSummary stays only as the rules' reference for tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019wwAR8vet2nCM1HhYR5VRz
